`$before` and `$after` wrap each direct child with a prefix and suffix.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    list #= [$before [:<li>], $after [:</li>]:
        <ul>
            [$slot]
        </ul>
    ]
]

This is useful for lists, table rows and repeated layout elements.

Either directive is optional, and each may appear once per head. Values must be
compile-time Strings or constant template wrappers. A constant template may
contain named slots, filled by the enclosing application. If a value contains a
slot, it must be named: an explicit default or positional slot is rejected. The
child insertion point is implicit.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    row #= [$html:<tr style="[$slot row_style]">]
    rows #= [$before row, $after [$html:</tr>]:[$slot]]

    [rows:
        [$in row_style:background: red;]
        [: first]
    ]
]

Conditions or loops producing no output do not emit a wrapper. An explicitly
selected empty String still does.

Use `$fresh` when one child should skip the immediate wrapper:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    [list:
        [: wrapped]
        [$fresh: [: not wrapped]]
    ]
]
